# {{ projectName }}

FastAPI foundation with process health routes. Product operations belong to this application.

## Run and verify

The canonical quality/build path uses Git, Make and Docker. Resolve and commit `uv.lock` once after a fresh render; existing checkouts enforce it. A native Python/uv loop is optional.

```bash
uv lock
make install
make CONTAINERIZED=1 run
```

`create_app` reads validated settings when called. Imports do not connect to the network. `GET /health/live` checks the process; `/health/ready` checks enabled required resources.{% if withPersistence %} Set `DATABASE_URL` to a `postgresql+asyncpg://` URL before normal startup. Migrations never run during application startup.{% else %} No DSN or credentials are needed.{% endif %}

```bash
make lint
make typecheck
{% if withTesting %}make test-unit
{% endif %}make build
```

{% if withTesting %}`make test` includes isolated runtime coverage{% if withPersistence %} and a real PostgreSQL transaction/readiness check requiring `TEST_DATABASE_URL` for an explicitly disposable database{% endif %}. Managed tests live in `tests/foundation`; `tests/test_http.py` is an application-owned seed.{% else %}Testing was disabled. Enable it before claiming test coverage or enabling CI.{% endif %}

{% if withDocker %}## Container

`make build` exports wheel/sdist from the Docker `artifacts` target; `make image` loads the runtime candidate. The runtime installs that wheel, uses UID 65532 and one Uvicorn process, and supports a read-only filesystem and bounded SIGTERM shutdown.
{% if withTesting %}
`make verify` freshly tests the installed wheel in a container{% if withPersistence %} with a unique disposable Compose PostgreSQL project{% endif %}. It cleans only its own resources. Installed coverage is written to `coverage/installed/`; source reports remain separate. Percentages are advisory; missing/stale reports and real check failures fail. A cached build never substitutes for executing tests.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}{% if withKubernetes %}## Kubernetes

`deploy/chart` is the shared FastAPI chart managed by Copier. Set `image.repository` and `image.digest` in the application-owned `deploy/values.yaml`; database values reference an existing Secret rather than containing credentials. `make chart-check chart` validates and packages the chart. Deploy the resulting checksummed artifact and the already tested image; deployment does not rebuild it. Optional migrations run as a Helm pre-install/pre-upgrade Job, never in every application replica. Application rollback does not undo a database migration.
{% if withDocker %}
`make deploy-local` creates a dedicated `{{ packageName }}-local` Kind cluster and `.local/kubeconfig`{% if withPersistence %}, including a synthetic disposable PostgreSQL{% endif %}. It loads the local candidate using an explicit development tag override. `make undeploy-local` removes only that cluster. It does not select an external kubeconfig.
{% endif %}{% endif %}

`PROJECT.md`, `SERVICE.md`, settings, migrations, seed tests and deployment values are application-owned. Review updates and provenance before applying them. See [architecture](docs/architecture.md) and [contribution guide](CONTRIBUTING.md). CI preserves artifacts and coverage; registry publication and release require separate configured targets and authorization.

